DO Resolve the requested ticket ID, absolute project, private absolute ix and
    acli executables, and the absolute ../assets directory beside this program.
    Let ix own task validation, snapshots, and initialization. Plain directories
    are supported; linked Git worktrees are not. Return an object with ticket_id,
    project, ix, acli, and assets. AS context

RUN @context.ix task --snapshot @context.project AS snapshot_result

DO Parse @snapshot_result.stdout as JSON. Verify its state is ok and return its
    opaque snapshot value. AS snapshot

RUN @context.acli jira workitem view @context.ticket_id --fields "key,issuetype,summary,status,assignee,description,attachment" --json AS jira_result

DO Parse @jira_result.stdout as JSON. Verify its key equals @context.ticket_id
    and the requested details are complete. Return the ticket object. AS ticket

SET ticket_layout = """
# TICKET-ID

Type: <type>
Summary: <summary>
Status: <status>
Assignee: <assignee or None>

## Description

<full description or None>

## Criteria

<explicit criteria or None>

## Attachments

- <filename> — <URL>
"""

DO Prepare ticket Markdown from @ticket using @ticket_layout. Preserve complete
    descriptions, lists, tables, and media links with supplied names and URLs.
    Keep unresolved references, invent no mappings or criteria, and use None for
    absent values or attachments. Return only the Markdown string and write
    nothing. AS ticket_markdown

RUN @context.ix task --expect @snapshot @context.assets @context.project AS workspace_result

DO Parse @workspace_result.stdout as JSON. Verify its state is ok and its files
    list contains ticket.md, estimate.md, and pr.md. Return an object with
    directory and the three absolute file paths. AS workspace

DO Write @ticket_markdown only to the empty ticket.md under
    @workspace.directory. Preserve Git exclusions and .gitignore. Do not copy,
    reread, or perform extra filesystem checks.

PRINT Report @context.ticket_id and @workspace's three absolute file paths briefly.
